          "page": 2,
          "excerpt": "MEETING IN LONDON ON THE EVE OF THE JULY 21 INTERNATIONAL MEETING ON BOSNIA, THE SECRETARY AND NATO SYG CLAES AGREED ON THE NEED TO ISSUE A WARNING TO THE BOSNIAN SERBS AGAINST FURTHER AGGRESSION AND TO RESPOND WITH STRATEGIC USE OF AIR POWER SHOULD THIS WARNING NOT BE OBSERVED. CLAES EXPRESSED CONCERN THAT IT WOULD BE DIFFICULT TO CONVINCE UNSYG BOUTROS GHALI TO WEAKEN THE EXISTING DUAL-KEY SYSTEM, AND THAT THERE MIGHT BE SOME OPPOSITION IN THE NAC TO MORE ROBUST USE OF AIR POWER. HE WOULD NOT WANT THE JULY 21 MEETING TO HAND OVER THE TASK IN BOSNIA TO NATO WITHOUT ALSO GIVING IT THE MEANS. THE SECRETARY NOTED THAT ONE PREREQUISITE FOR A MORE ROBUST COURSE IN BOSNIA--AGREEMENT AMONG THE …",
