          "excerpt": "ON JULY 12 BOSNIAN FOREIGN MINISTER SACIRBEY MET WITH SYG CLAES TO DISCUSS THE BOSNIAN GOVERNMENT'S VIEWS ON THE WAR'S DYNAMICS AND UNPROFOR'S FUTURE ROLE, IN LIGHT OF RECENT DEVELOPMENTS IN SREBRENICA. (SEE FULL TEXT IN PARAGRAPH 3 BELOW). SACIRBEY MAINTAINED THAT GOBH WOULD ASK UNPROFOR TO LEAVE IF IT COULD NOT RESTORE THE SREBRENICA SAFE AREA. THE BOSNIAN SERBS WERE NOW ENCOURAGED TO THREATEN THE OTHER SAFE AREAS, MOST NOTABLY ZEPA, MAKING THEIR DEFENSE UNTENABLE. SACIRBEY ASSERTED THAT CURRENTLY, UNPROFOR HARDLY PERFORMED A POSITIVE ROLE, PROVIDING ONLY A SOURCE OF HOSTAGES AND BLACKMAIL, WHICH REINFORCED GOBH'S VIEW THAT UNPROFOR MUST LEAVE AS A STEP TOWARDS LIFTING THE ARMS EMBARGO. …",
