          "page": 2,
          "excerpt": "AT AJULY 17 INFORMAL MEETING OF PERMREPS, SYG CLAES, CMC, AND SACEUR, DUTCH CHARGE P.C. FEITH SAID THAT THE CONFIBENTFAL CONMBEN FAL PAGE 02 USNATO 02945 1717422 DUTCH PEACEKEEPERS RELEASED FROM SREBRENICA HAD BEEN REQUIRED BY DUTCH AUTHORITIES TO KEEP SILENT ON WHAT THEY HAD EXPERIENCED. THERE IS \"CLEAR SUSPICION\" OF \"GENOCIDE ON A FAIRLY LARGE SCALE\" BY BOSNIAN SERB ARMY (BSA) FORCES. IMMEDIATELY AFTER SREBRENICA FELL, BSA TROOPS BEHAVED CORRECTLY, BUT AS NIGHT FELL THEY BEGAN DRINKING, AND MURDERS ENSUED, THE DUTCH ARE CONCERNED THAT, IF THIS INFORMATION WERE ATTRIBUTED TO DUTCH FORCES, IT COULD JEOPARDIZE THE 300 TROOPS STILL IN THE AREA UNTIL THE END OF THIS WEEK. HUNTER NNNN …",
