      "pageEvidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "excerpt": "SPEAKING JULY 13, CROATIAN FM GRANIC USED THE FALL OF SREBRENICA TO REINFORCE THE POINT HE HAS BEEN MAKING FOR SOME TIME, THAT BELGRADE IS RESPONSIBLE AND THE INTERNATIONAL COMMUNITY MUST EXERT STRONG PRESSURE ON MILOSEVIC. OVERALL, GRANIC'S MESSAGE WAS ONE OF REASSURANCE THAT CROATIA REMAINED COMMITTED TO PEACEFUL RESOLUTION OF THE REGION'S PROBLEMS AND RESTRAINT IN THE FACE OF PROVOCATION. BUT HE DID LAY DOWN MARKERS CONCERNING UNCRO'S NONPERFORMANCE OF ITS MANDATE AND POSSIBLE SERB MILITARY THREATS TO BIHAC. REFERRING TO EVIDENCE OF A SERB BUILDUP AROUND BIHAC, HE MADE CLEAR THIS WOULD BE OF MUCH MORE DIRECT CONCERN TO CROATIA, AND COULD LEAD TO A\"WIDENING OF THE WAR,\" THOUGH HE STOPPED …",
          "note": "Extracted body text; verify against facsimile"
        }
      ],
