          "excerpt": "STATUS OF DISPLACED PERSONS: AS OF 1800 ON JULY 13, UNPF SENIOR POLITICAL ADVISOR ALMSTROM REPORTED THAT APPROXLMATELY 5500 DPS WERE AT THE TUZLA AIR BASE AND ANOTHER 6000 AT KLADANJ. THAT WAS THE RESULT OF THE FIRST DAY'S PROCESSING, MEANING THAT MLADIC WAS MOVING ABOUT 10,000 PEOPLE A DAY. THOSE WHO HAD ARRIVED SO FAR WERE ALL CHILDREN, WOMEN, OR ELDERLY. IT WAS CLEAR THAT MILITARY AGE MEN WERE BEING SEPARATED OUT AND DETAINED. AT TUZLA, PEOPLE WERE LIVING IN TENTS ON THE RUNWAY; DEHYDRATION WAS THE MAIN PROBLEM. ALMSTROM SAID THAT THE UN HAD ENOUGH FOOD FOR SEVERAL DAYS AVAILABLE IN BELGRADE, TUZLA, AND ZENICA. NOTHING HAD REACHED SREBRENICA YET, ALTHOUGH AS WE SPOKE HE RECEIVED …",
